  "result": "Subcommands now receive their own section of `default_map`. Before this fix, `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` never reached `runserver`, so `--port` fell back to 8000.\n\n**Cause:** In `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a subcommand context copied the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry keyed by its name.\n\n**Fix:** The subcommand context now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. It only uses that value when it is a mapping, so a non-dict entry such as `True` or `UNSET` under a command name doesn't break lookups.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Full test suite: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, no failures.\n- A new regression test, `test_default_map_applies_to_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`, checks that `runserver` picks up `port=5000` from the nested map.\n- I kept the CRLF line endings the files already use.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry or commit anything. Say if you want either.",
